What I did: Fixed an information gap in context_bar (src/format/cost.rs). It clamped its percentage label at a flat 100% for any usage ≥ max, so a genuinely over-budget context was indistinguishable from one sitting exactly at the limit — the same class of bug as issue #263's <1% fix, just at the other end of the scale.

The fix: The bar fill stays clamped (never over-draws past full), but the label now uses the true unclamped percentage, so an over-budget context reads 150% instead of a misleading 100%.

Verification (test-first): Wrote three tests before implementing — over-budget shows the true percentage with a fully-filled bar, and exactly-full still reads a clean 100%. All 4269 tests pass; cargo fmt, cargo clippy -D warnings, `cargo build, cargo test` all green.

